{"model": "gpt-oss-120b", "input": [{"role": "developer", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Assess the full current SHACL using these distinct inputs:\n- Regulation establishes the represented obligation.\n- Declared schema/mappings establish RDF identifiers, ownership, paths, datatypes and units; a similar label is not an equivalent mapping.\n- Approved scope establishes declared external research assumptions, not real-vessel certification. Conditions inside the represented requirement remain in scope.\n- Candidate code is what you assess, not source/schema evidence.\n- Execution diagnostics establish observed technical behavior, not regulatory correctness or full coverage.\n\nProcedure:\n1. Read the represented requirement and approved scope.\n2. Compare its conditions and obligations with the full current code, including activation, query branches and supplied changes/removals.\n3. Report supported code defects as issues with actionable corrections. Preserve unaffected obligations; do not propose deletion just to pass checks.\n4. Report genuinely missing or contradictory information as context questions, without inventing a code defect.\n5. Explicitly address every carried-forward question using question_review; use current supplied evidence to support resolution/withdrawal. STILL_UNRESOLVED remains blocking.\n6. Return one complete JSON object matching expected_response_schema and its authoritative description. Make assessment consistent with issues, questions, carried-forward questions and change/gap assessments. Delivery is separate from approval.\n\nEvidence references identify supplied E entries only. Generic evidence-field example: \"evidence\":[\"E7\"] (valid only if E7 is supplied). Optional evidence character spans refer to that entry, not code; asserted quotations must match exactly. RDF_FACT references cite the whole atomic fact.\nCode locations belong in issues[].location. Generic location-field example: \"location\":{\"start\":1,\"end\":1,\"unit\":\"lines\"} (valid only if current line 1 exists). Software extracts exact code and binds hashes; do not quote code or invent an evidence ID such as candidate_shape. Missing constraints use a real insertion anchor. Context questions/dispositions need no code location.\n\nCitations support claims, not their interpretation. Regulation need not contain RDF IRIs; mappings do not establish formulas or compliance answers. Keep missing mappings unresolved. Proposed representation changes must pair each operand's declared property/path/role; unit renaming is not conversion. Review supplied prior issues and functional changes/removals, including reachable replacements, using the documented conditional fields. Software owns IDs and bookkeeping.\n\nFailed responses authorize no repair and create no accepted issues. For a response correction, keep the same candidate, evidence and original prior state; return the complete corrected review. Never request evaluation fixtures, labels, counterparts or historical solutions.\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "{\"candidate_version\": 1, \"candidate_sha256\": \"9968fd2a5a45f63b1adf56de5b7aa763c57326d204c20f4ca186dc1635658d84\", \"review_request_id\": \"review:c96e4ce61da774323dd0335a49aa1bafc0cbd508a4aadeb8427a49615bae7da5\", \"full_candidate\": \"@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n\\n# Shape that enforces the allowed ice‑class values defined in\\n# TRF‑010 clause 1.8 (Ice classes) of the Ice Class Regulations\\n# (2021 edition, file data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt, SHA‑256 e0bf…e8ba).\\n\\nnltl:ShipIceClassShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\\n    rdfs:comment \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Requirement TRF‑010, clause 1.8:\\n    “Under section 3 of the Act on the Ice Classes of Ships and Icebreaker Assistance (1121/2005),\\n    ships are assigned to ice classes as follows:\\n      1. ice class IA Super …\\n      2. ice class IA …\\n      3. ice class IB …\\n      4. ice class IC …\\n      5. ice class II …\\n      6. ice class III …”\\n    The shape requires every instance of nltl:ship to have an iceClass property whose\\n    value is one of the six enumerated ice‑class concepts.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\" ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:iceClass ;\\n        sh:in (\\n            nltl:iceClassIaSuper\\n            nltl:iceClassIa\\n            nltl:iceClassIb\\n            nltl:iceClassIc\\n            nltl:iceClassIi\\n            nltl:iceClassIii\\n        ) ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Ship must be assigned one of the ice‑class values defined in TRF‑010 clause 1.8 (IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, III).\\\" ;\\n        sh:severity sh:Violation ;\\n    ] .\\n\\n# Enumeration individuals (exact IRIs as declared in the ontology)\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIaSuper a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"IA Super\\\"@en .\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIa a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"IA\\\"@en .\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIb a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"IB\\\"@en .\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIc a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"IC\\\"@en .\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIi a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"II\\\"@en .\\n\\nnltl:iceClassIii a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"III\\\"@en .\\n\", \"previous_candidate\": null, \"max_issues\": 12, \"expected_response_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"assessment\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"APPROVE\", \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\", \"REJECT\"]}, \"issues\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"quote\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8}, \"location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"lines\", \"characters\"]}}, \"required\": [\"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"suggestion\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"operands\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"property\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"minItems\": 1}, \"role\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PROPERTY\", \"NUMERIC_OPERAND\"]}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"datatype\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"property\", \"path\", \"role\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"evidence\", \"location\", \"suggestion\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 12}, \"questions\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"missing\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"why\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"source\", \"schema\"]}, \"reference\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 100}, \"section\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"quote\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}]}, \"maxItems\": 8}}, \"required\": [\"missing\", \"why\", \"kind\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 3}, \"gap_review\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"enum\": [\"G1\", \"G2\", \"G3\", \"G4\", \"G5\"]}, \"material\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"why\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"material\", \"why\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 5}}, \"required\": [\"assessment\", \"issues\", \"questions\", \"gap_review\"], \"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Return complete assessment, issues and questions. APPROVE requires no current/prior issue or material question, all changes SUPPORTED and every supplied gap explicitly nonmaterial. REJECT needs an actionable code issue. HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED needs a new/carried-forward material question or unresolved change/gap. Issue fields: description, evidence, location, suggestion. Evidence uses supplied E IDs or {id,start?,end?,quote?}; paired start/end are character offsets in that evidence, not code. RDF_FACT citations use the whole fact. Optional quotes are checked exactly. location uses start/end and optional unit=lines (default) or characters, on the full current candidate; software extracts exact code. Context questions/dispositions have no location and need no invented defect. Assess each supplied C ID once. REGRESSION links an actionable zero-based issue index; UNRESOLVED blocks approval. For APPROVE assess each G ID with material=false and why; material gaps require questions. Software owns hashes, IDs and reconciliation. Review supplied prior issues without returning duplicate bookkeeping. Unsupported assertions, invented references/quotes and inconsistent decisions are invalid; citation interpretation remains model judgment.\"}, \"execution_probe\": {\"candidate_version\": 1, \"candidate_sha256\": \"9968fd2a5a45f63b1adf56de5b7aa763c57326d204c20f4ca186dc1635658d84\", \"engine\": \"pyshacl\", \"engine_version\": \"0.31.0\", \"engine_outcome\": \"COMPLETED_NO_ENGINE_ERROR\", \"diagnostic_availability\": \"Captured verbatim\", \"activation\": {\"roots\": [\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ShipIceClassShape\"], \"reachable\": [\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ShipIceClassShape\", \"n9b54f4aa7ca34c0a968116d5f70fbe4ab1\"], \"enforcing_nodes\": [\"n9b54f4aa7ca34c0a968116d5f70fbe4ab1\"], \"deactivated_reachable\": [], \"orphan_constraint_nodes\": [], \"unsupported_custom_targets\": [], \"supported\": true}, \"regulatory_correctness_established\": false, \"scope\": \"Execution-only schema-derived probe; no expected regulatory verdict; success is not complete correctness\", \"diagnostics\": {\"stdout\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stdout\"}, \"stderr\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stderr\"}}}, \"citation_format\": {\"evidence\": \"E ID, optional character span. Server resolves exact text/hash/provenance. quote optional and checked if asserted.\", \"code\": \"location {start,end,unit?}; default one-based inclusive lines, optional characters half-open. Server binds version/hash.\", \"roles\": \"SOURCE: obligation. SCHEMA_TEXT/RDF_FACT: representation. CALLER_DECLARATION: external research population. No legal IRI requirement; no formulas inferred from mappings.\"}, \"protocol_version\": 2, \"context\": {\"requirement\": {\"id\": \"TRF-010\", \"source\": \"Ice Class Regulations and the Application Thereof\", \"clause\": \"1.8\"}, \"scope\": \"Implement and review the supplied source in the declared schema. No supplied compliance solution or expected verdict. Material unspecified representation/applicability prevents acceptance. External population/date eligibility and edition selection are supplied by caller admission, not independently inferred from RDF. Conditions within the represented requirement remain in scope; activation and query correctness are separate obligations.\", \"source_selection\": {\"manifest_sha256\": \"b01f80a76556eed28d24921cef1c7f5503db00a54a3ef6139edd1678b7e6e1aa\", \"included_characters\": 65326, \"original_characters\": 169151, \"omitted_sections\": 210, \"retrieval\": \"Schema.source_evidence(file, document_sha256, start, end); complete sections/hashes retained in source_selection_manifest.json; missing necessary evidence must remain unresolved\"}, \"source_completeness\": \"Deterministic source selection, not a proof of complete context. Ambiguous primary anchors retain full source; unresolved references require review.\"}, \"admission_sha256\": \"96bdce430721d1ee206851148bd5f514d992b526e7e54c1f14517948046f6846\", \"evidence_catalog\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"catalog_sha256\": \"690197d7ada8120be652ead15c8711e5e798c4f1c18780baa124a03c47f0ed7a\", \"entries\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"E1\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputComplianceMethod> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-009\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E2\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaFactorF1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E3\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputFactorCd> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N4 - explicit engineering quantity in ASCII lowerCamelCase; formula symbols remain aliases only.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E4\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Navigating in ice\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E5\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ownerRequested2008EngineOutputRequirements> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E6\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ownerRequested2008EngineOutputRequirements> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E7\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-004\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E8\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"               Table 6-10: Default values for prime mover maximum torque Qemax\\n                Propeller type                                  Qemax\\n                Propellers driven by electric motor             *Qmotor\\n                CP propellers not driven by electric motor      Qn\\n                FP propellers driven by turbine                 Qn\\n                FP propellers driven by diesel engine           0.75 Qn\\n\\n*Qmotor is the electric motor peak torque.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 112803, \"end\": 113275}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E9\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ownerRequested2008EngineOutputRequirements> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-R7-0007\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E10\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-074\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E11\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Ice class\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E12\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaFactorF3> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E13\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"iceClass\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E14\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-102\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E15\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassIaSuper> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E16\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#markingPlainlyVisibleInIceConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Marking plainly visible in ice conditions\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E17\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Other waters ice condition represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E18\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#propulsionMachineryContinuousOutput\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"QuantityProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Propulsion machinery continuous output\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"propulsionMachineryContinuousOutput\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-017 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 3.1\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"kW\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E19\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassIa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E20\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputComplianceMethodValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Engine output compliance method value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E21\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaFactorF3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E22\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-169\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E23\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientB> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-209\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E24\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaFactorF3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Engine output formula factor f3\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E25\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hydraulicPropulsionMachinery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Hydraulic propulsion machinery\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E26\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceReference> \\\"IMO26-002 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.2 | Chapter 9-1 applicability; IMO26-016 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.5 | Chapter 11-1 applicability\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E27\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N1 - reuse only after exact URI and semantic-context verification\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E28\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E29\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputCoefficientKe> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for engineOutputCoefficientKe derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E30\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaBasePowerP0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Engine output formula base power p0\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E31\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-020\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E32\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientK> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E33\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientB> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E34\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaFactorF4\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"QuantityProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Engine output formula factor f4\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"engineOutputFormulaFactorF4\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-132 | TRAFICOM p.64 | 8\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E35\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputComplianceMethodValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Engine output compliance method value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E36\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hydraulicPropulsionMachinery> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N6 - concise ASCII lowerCamelCase controlled-value name grounded in the linked regulation.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E37\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputRegulationEdition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassRegulationEditionValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E38\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientA> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"coefficientA\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E39\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                                       6     Frames extending from the tank\\n                                             top to the main deck of a single-\\n                                             decked vessel\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 56122, \"end\": 56340}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E40\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E41\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                 Table 6-15: Value of the parameter G for different m/k ratios.\\n              m/k     G        m/k          G          m/k          G\\n              3       6        6.5          1871       10           3.629·106\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 139831, \"end\": 140059}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E42\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Benchmark entity\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E43\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E44\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E45\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#propulsionMachineryContinuousOutput> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-017\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E46\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0270\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E47\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                   Table 6-8: Default values for hydrodynamic bollard thrust, T\\n                Propeller type                                      T\\n                CP propellers (open)                                1.25 Tn\\n                CP propellers (ducted)                              1.1 Tn\\n                FP propellers driven by turbine or electric motor   Tn\\n                FP propellers driven by diesel engine (open)        0.85 Tn\\n                FP propellers driven by diesel engine (ducted)      0.75 Tn\\n\\nHere Tn is the nominal propeller thrust at MCR in the free running open water condition.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 107757, \"end\": 108372}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E48\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientB> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E49\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputComplianceMethod\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Engine output compliance method\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"engineOutputComplianceMethod\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputComplianceMethodValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-007 | TRAFICOM p.5 | 1.6; TRF-009 | TRAFICOM p.6 | 1.7; TRF-024 | TRAFICOM p.10 | 3.2.4\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E50\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"cargoShip\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E51\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0350\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E52\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaDisplacement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E53\", \"kind\": \"CONTEXT_STATUS\", \"text\": \"[]\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"unresolvedOwnership\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E54\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-039\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E55\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputFactorCd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E56\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputCoefficientKe> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical dimensionless unit\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E57\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Ship size engine output coefficient a\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E58\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientK> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Ship size engine output coefficient k is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E59\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipSizeEngineOutputCoefficientK> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Numeric operand, comparison value, formula input/output, or engineering measurement.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E60\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E61\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                           Table 6-4: Load cases for open propellers.\\n              Force             Loaded area                        Right-handed propeller\\n                                                                   blade seen from behind\\nLoad case 1   Fb                Uniform pressure applied on the\\n                                blade back (suction side) to an\\n                                area from 0.6R to the tip and\\n                                from the leading edge to 0.2\\n                                times the chord length.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nLoad case 2   50 % of Fb        Uniform pressure applied on the\\n                                blade back (suction side) on the\\n                                blade tip area outside 0.9R ra-\\n                                dius.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nLoad case 3   Ff                Uniform pressure applied on the\\n                                blade face (pressure side) to an\\n                                area from 0.6R to the tip and\\n                                from the leading edge to 0.2\\n                                times the chord length.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nLoad case 4   50% of Ff         Uniform pressure applied on the\\n                                blade face (pressure side) of the\\n                                blade tip area outside 0.9R ra-\\n                                dius.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nLoad case 5   60% of Ff or      Uniform pressure applied on the\\n              Fb, whichever     blade face (pressure side) to an\\n              is greater        area from 0.6R to the tip and\\n                                from the trailing edge to 0.2\\n                                times the chord length.\\n\\f                                                                                                                    Regulation\\n                                                                                                                         34 (65)\\n                                                                                          TRAFICOM/68863/03.04.01.00/2021\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 94711, \"end\": 96747}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E62\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaDisplacement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Engine output formula displacement\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E63\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-066\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E64\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"For category A and B ships other than oil tankers constructed on or after 1 January 2017, all cargo tanks constructed and utilized to carry oil shall be separated from the outer shell by a distance of not less than 0.76 m.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E65\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassValue\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Finnish-Swedish ice-class value\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"iceClassValue\\\", \\\"mapping_basis\\\": \\\"Ontology declaration (registry row not required)\\\", \\\"types\\\": [\\\"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class\\\"]}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E66\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Pleasure yacht\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E67\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#engineOutputFormulaBasePowerP0> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-132\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E68\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E69\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\":